WEBVTT

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.680
Aircraft lighting serves different purposes.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.000
Anti-collision lighting helps make the drone visible to the operator and others.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.235
Orientation lights help distinguish the aircraft's front, rear, or sides.

00:00:10.235 --> 00:00:13.205
Requirements and approved configurations depend on the operation and current rules.

00:00:13.205 --> 00:00:17.000
Lighting must be visible enough for its intended purpose without creating excessive glare

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:17.945
for the pilot,

00:00:17.945 --> 00:00:18.965
camera, crew, or other people.

00:00:18.965 --> 00:00:21.965
Verify operation, brightness settings, attachment security,

00:00:21.965 --> 00:00:25.215
and visibility from relevant directions before launch.

00:00:25.215 --> 00:00:28.875
Additional lights consume power and can affect weight, balance, aerodynamics,

00:00:28.875 --> 00:00:29.945
or sensor behavior.

00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:33.880
Include them in battery planning and confirm that mounting does not obstruct navigation,

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.195
cooling, cameras, or required indicators.

00:00:36.195 --> 00:00:37.968
Background lights can confuse identification.

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:40.560
Streetlights, vehicles, buildings, towers, stars,

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.945
and reflections may resemble or hide aircraft lights.

00:00:42.945 --> 00:00:46.875
Choose crew positions and routes that preserve a clear visual reference and avoid visually

00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:48.965
crowded backgrounds where practical.

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:53.250
Recognizing a colored light does not always establish aircraft attitude.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.000
Perspective, distance, turns, and partial obstruction can change what is visible.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.225
Cross-check movement, telemetry, route, and multiple cues before commanding a correction.

00:01:01.225 --> 00:01:04.060
Lighting is a risk control, not permission to extend distance,

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:06.965
operate beyond visual capability, or ignore obstacles.

00:01:06.965 --> 00:01:09.525
If required lighting fails, becomes obscured,

00:01:09.525 --> 00:01:11.945
or no longer supports reliable identification,

00:01:11.945 --> 00:01:14.000
follow the planned abort and landing procedure.
